From 2283e5e1b289d37c292e8ab512bdd7381fc77430 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tian Zheng <zhengtian10@huawei.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 07:15:38 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] KVM: Add the dirty ring size hook stub

kvm_vm_ioctl_enable_dirty_log_ring() is built for every architecture,
but the kvm_arch_dirty_ring_size_updated() prototype sits in the
CONFIG_HAVE_KVM_DIRTY_RING branch and the weak definition lives in
the config-gated dirty_ring.o, so architectures without the dirty
ring fail to build.

Add the missing stub.

Signed-off-by: AkiraZheng <1428384878@qq.com>
---
 include/linux/kvm_dirty_ring.h | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/include/linux/kvm_dirty_ring.h b/include/linux/kvm_dirty_ring.h
index c2b922791530..7492858cbe0a 100644
--- a/include/linux/kvm_dirty_ring.h
+++ b/include/linux/kvm_dirty_ring.h
@@ -70,6 +70,10 @@ static inline void kvm_dirty_ring_free(struct kvm_dirty_ring *ring)
 {
 }
 
+static inline void kvm_arch_dirty_ring_size_updated(struct kvm *kvm)
+{
+}
+
 #else /* CONFIG_HAVE_KVM_DIRTY_RING */
 
 int kvm_cpu_dirty_log_size(struct kvm *kvm);
-- 
2.43.0

